PaddleOCR 3.3.x (optional dependency, kb-rag-parser local OCR fallback, M8)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
License: Apache-2.0 (both paddleocr and its runtime dependency
paddlepaddle). No conflict with this project's Apache-2.0 license.
Status: integrated in M8 as an OPTIONAL dependency of kb-rag-parser
(`requirements-ocr.txt`, pinned to paddlepaddle==3.3.1 + paddleocr==3.3.3;
not installed by default, to keep the base image small). It is toggled by
the parser environment variable `OCR_ENGINE=none|paddle` (default `none`,
which leaves pre-M8 behavior unchanged); `OCR_ENGINE=paddle` without the
optional dependencies installed fails fast at startup with an actionable
error. When enabled, scanned pages rendered by the parser are OCR'd
locally with the ch_PP-OCRv4 model and marked `ocr_source: paddle`, and
kb-rag-server then skips the hosted vision-model call for those pages
(fallback order: server-side VLM if an API key is configured -> local
PaddleOCR -> skip with degradation counter; see M8-CONTRACTS.md §0 point 4).
This serves offline/air-gapped deployments where no vision model API is
reachable. PP-OCRv4 model weights are NOT redistributed in this
repository; they are downloaded on first use from the upstream model
source (HuggingFace by default, or ModelScope via
`PADDLE_PDX_MODEL_SOURCE=ModelScope`), so fully offline deployments must
pre-seed the model cache directory.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Alibaba Cloud DashScope qwen-vl-max (hosted vision-language model service, M3)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Nature: this is a remote, hosted model API (Alibaba Cloud DashScope),
not a bundled or redistributed piece of open-source software, and no
DashScope source code or model weights are contained in this repository.
It is called over HTTPS through the same Provider abstraction (D14) used
for every other model capability (embedding/rerank/chat/vision), so it is
disclosed here in the same spirit as the other third-party dependencies
in this NOTICE file: usage of this project may depend on it, and its own
terms of service (Alibaba Cloud DashScope service agreement) apply
independently of this project's Apache-2.0 license.
Usage in this project (see M3-CONTRACTS.md §3.1): kb-rag-server calls the
DashScope OpenAI-compatible `chat/completions` endpoint with model
`VISION_MODEL` (default `qwen-vl-max`) to (a) transcribe text on scanned
pages that kb-parser rendered to an image (unless, from M8 on, the page
was already OCR'd by the optional local PaddleOCR fallback — see the
PaddleOCR entry above), and (b) generate a text proxy (description
+ OCR transcript) for embedded/standalone images. kb-rag-parser itself
never calls qwen-vl or any other model provider (docs/M3-CONTRACTS.md §0/§1).
Not a hard dependency lock-in: per D14, an OpenAI-compatible VisionProvider
implementation is also available so self-hosted or alternative vision
models can be used instead of DashScope.

